```java
public static int countOccurrences(String str, String target) {
    int count = 0;
    int index = str.indexOf(target);
    while (index != -1) {
        count++;
        str = str.substring(index + target.length());
        index = str.indexOf(target);
    }
    return count;
}

public static String removeFirst(String str, String target) {
    int i = str.indexOf(target);
    if (i == -1) {
        return str;
    }
    return str.substring(0, i) + str.substring(i + target.length());
}
```

In part (a), each time target is found, the search continues in the part of str after the match, so occurrences don't overlap ("aaaa" with "aa" gives 2). The loop ends when indexOf returns −1. In part (b), the result joins the text before the match with the text after it.
